(>> Solution to Question 1:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the biochemical architecture of Cyclin-Dependent Kinases \(CDKs\) and detail the dual structural mechanism of CDK activation by Cyclin binding and CAK phosphorylation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Biochemical Architecture and Dual Activation Mechanism of CDKs:) Tj
T*
(   1. Structural Architecture of Inactive Monomeric CDKs \(e.g., CDK2\):) Tj
T*
(   - CDKs possess a standard two-lobed protein kinase fold: an N-terminal lobe dominated by) Tj
T*
(   antiparallel beta-sheets containing the ATP-binding pocket and conserved PSTAIRE alpha-helix,) Tj
T*
(   and a C-terminal lobe primarily composed of alpha-helices.) Tj
T*
(   - In the monomeric, inactive ground state, access to the catalytic active site is physically) Tj
T*
(   obstructed by an extended flexible peptide loop \(~20 amino acids\) called the T-loop \(activation) Tj
T*
(   loop\).) Tj
T*
(   - In addition, critical catalytic residues are misaligned: the PSTAIRE helix is tilted outward,) Tj
T*
(   rotating a critical glutamate \(Glu-51\) away from the catalytic lysine \(Lys-33\), preventing ATP) Tj
T*
(   phosphate coordination.) Tj
T*
(   2. Step 1: Activation by Cyclin Binding:) Tj
T*
(   - When a regulatory Cyclin partner \(e.g., Cyclin A\) binds to the PSTAIRE helix and surrounding) Tj
T*
(   regions on the N-lobe, it forces the PSTAIRE helix to rotate inward by 90 degrees.) Tj
T*
(   - This reorients Glu-51 to form an essential electrostatic salt bridge with Lys-33, correctly) Tj
T*
(   positioning the alpha- and beta-phosphates of ATP.) Tj
T*
(   - Concurrently, cyclin binding causes the T-loop to swing 20 A out of the catalytic cleft,) Tj
T*
(   partially exposing the substrate-binding groove. This conformational transition confers basal) Tj
T*
(   \(~1%\) kinase activity.) Tj
T*
(   3. Step 2: Full Activation by CAK \(CDK-Activating Kinase\) Phosphorylation:) Tj
T*
(   - CDK-Activating Kinase \(a trimeric complex of CDK7, Cyclin H, and Mat1\) phosphorylates a) Tj
T*
(   single conserved threonine residue localized near the apex of the displaced T-loop \(Thr-160 in) Tj
T*
(   human CDK2, Thr-161 in CDK1, Thr-172 in CDK4\).) Tj
T*
(   - The newly introduced negatively charged phosphate group forms an electrostatic coordination) Tj
T*
(   triad with three invariant basic residues \(Arg-50, Arg-126, Arg-150\).) Tj
T*
(   - This acts as an organizing center that locks the T-loop into a rigid, open conformation,) Tj
T*
(   creating the complete, high-affinity peptide substrate-binding cleft and elevating catalytic) Tj
T*
(   efficiency \(kcat/Km\) by > 300-fold.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 2:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the Retinoblastoma \(Rb\) - E2F pathway governing the G1/S restriction point and explain how bistable switching ensures irreversible S-phase commitment.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Retinoblastoma \(Rb\) - E2F Pathway and Bistable Switching at the Restriction Point:) Tj
T*
(   1. The G1 Restriction Point \(R-Point\):) Tj
T*
(   The restriction point is the critical temporal boundary in late G1 phase beyond which the cell) Tj
T*
(   is irreversibly committed to replicate its DNA and complete division, even if extracellular) Tj
T*
(   growth factors are completely withdrawn.) Tj
T*
(   2. The Hypo-Phosphorylated Rb Gatekeeper State:) Tj
T*
(   - In quiescent \(G0\) and early G1 cells, the unphosphorylated or mono-phosphorylated) Tj
T*
(   Retinoblastoma tumor suppressor protein \(pRb\) binds tightly to heterodimers of E2F) Tj
T*
(   transcription factors \(E2F1, E2F2, E2F3\) and their DP partners \(DP1/2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Physical binding of Rb to the transactivation domain of E2F directly blocks transcription of) Tj
T*
(   S-phase genes.) Tj
T*
(   - Furthermore, Rb actively recruits chromatin-modifying corepressors: Histone Deacetylases) Tj
T*
(   \(HDAC1/2\), Histone Methyltransferases \(SUV39H1\), and the SWI/SNF nucleosome-remodeling complex,) Tj
T*
(   inducing a closed, transcriptionally silenced heterochromatin state at E2F-responsive) Tj
T*
ET

