(Lovely Professional University | Biotechnology Question Bank & Solutions) Tj
340 0 Td
(Page 13 of 32) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
45 780 Td
(   promoters.) Tj
T*
(   3. Mitogenic Signaling and Initial Phosphorylation:) Tj
T*
(   - Extracellular growth factors \(EGF, PDGF\) trigger the Ras-Raf-MEK-ERK signaling cascade,) Tj
T*
(   inducing transcriptional expression of D-type cyclins \(Cyclin D1, D2, D3\).) Tj
T*
(   - Cyclin D binds CDK4 and CDK6, phosphorylating Rb at specific C-terminal serine residues) Tj
T*
(   \(Ser-780, Ser-795\).) Tj
T*
(   - Initial phosphorylation causes Rb to dissociate from HDACs, relieving active repression,) Tj
T*
(   allowing low-level basal transcription of E2F target genes, notably Cyclin E and Cyclin A.) Tj
T*
(   4. The Hyper-Phosphorylated Bistable Switch:) Tj
T*
(   - Newly synthesized Cyclin E complexes with CDK2. Cyclin E-CDK2 phosphorylates Rb at multiple) Tj
T*
(   additional serine/threonine sites \(> 14 sites total\), fully hyper-phosphorylating Rb.) Tj
T*
(   - Hyper-phosphorylated Rb undergoes an intramolecular domain clasp between its N-terminus and) Tj
T*
(   pocket domain, completely destroying its binding affinity for E2F.) Tj
T*
(   - Free E2F rapidly drives massive transcription of S-phase genes: DNA Polymerase alpha, PCNA,) Tj
T*
(   MCM helicase, Thymidine Kinase, and crucially, Cyclin E itself!) Tj
T*
(   - This creates two self-reinforcing, irreversible positive feedback loops: \(1\) E2F) Tj
T*
(   transactivates its own gene; \(2\) E2F drives Cyclin E synthesis, which activates CDK2, which) Tj
T*
(   hyper-phosphorylates more Rb to free more E2F.) Tj
T*
(   - Once total Rb phosphorylation exceeds ~80%, the system flips into an autonomous, bistable) Tj
T*
(   'ON' state that can no longer be reversed by mitogen withdrawal.) Tj
T*
() Tj
