(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the bistable biochemical circuitry of Mitosis Promoting Factor \(MPF / Cyclin B-CDK1\) activation at the G2/M transition.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Bistable Switching and Systems Biology of MPF Activation at the G2/M Transition:) Tj
T*
(   1. The G2 Dormant Reservoir State:) Tj
T*
(   Throughout G2 phase, newly synthesized Cyclin B binds CDK1 \(Cdc2\). However, this nascent MPF) Tj
T*
(   complex is maintained in an enzymatically inactive state by dual inhibitory phosphorylation:) Tj
T*
(   - Wee1 Kinase phosphorylates Tyrosine-15 \(Tyr-15\) in the ATP-binding glycine-rich loop.) Tj
T*
