(   - Myt1 Kinase phosphorylates adjacent Threonine-14 \(Thr-14\).) Tj
T*
(   - These negative charges sterically interfere with ATP phosphate orientation, holding MPF) Tj
T*
(   inactive despite activating Thr-161 phosphorylation by CAK.) Tj
T*
(   2. Triggering Mitotic Entry:) Tj
T*
(   As cells achieve critical cell mass and complete DNA replication, Plk1 \(Polo-Like Kinase 1\) is) Tj
T*
(   activated:) Tj
T*
(   - Plk1 phosphorylates the dual-specificity phosphatase Cdc25C, partially activating it, and) Tj
T*
(   phosphorylates Wee1, marking it for degradation.) Tj
T*
(   - Active Cdc25C dephosphorylates Thr-14 and Tyr-15 on CDK1, generating a small initial pool of) Tj
T*
(   active Cyclin B-CDK1.) Tj
T*
(   3. Two Mutual Positive Feedback Loops \(The Hysteresis Engine\):) Tj
T*
(   Once this initial active CDK1 appears, it drives two explosive, interlocking positive feedback) Tj
T*
(   loops:) Tj
T*
(   - Positive Feedback Loop 1 \(CDK1 -> Cdc25C\): Active CDK1 directly phosphorylates Cdc25C on) Tj
T*
(   multiple N-terminal regulatory serines, increasing its phosphatase activity by > 20-fold! More) Tj
T*
(   active Cdc25C rapidly dephosphorylates more CDK1.) Tj
T*
(   - Double-Negative \(Positive\) Feedback Loop 2 \(CDK1 -| Wee1\): Active CDK1 directly) Tj
T*
(   phosphorylates Wee1 kinase on its N-terminal regulatory domain, inactivating its kinase) Tj
T*
(   function and creating a phosphodegron recognized by SCF-beta-TrCP for rapid) Tj
T*
(   ubiquitin-proteasome destruction.) Tj
T*
(   4. Greatwall Kinase and Phosphatase Suppression \(The Ensa/PP2A Switch\):) Tj
T*
(   In interphase, the counteracting phosphatase PP2A-B55 continuously dephosphorylates CDK1) Tj
T*
(   substrates, preventing mitotic entry:) Tj
T*
(   - Active CDK1 phosphorylates and activates Greatwall Kinase \(GWL / MASTL\).) Tj
T*
(   - GWL phosphorylates the small heat-stable proteins Ensa and ARPP19.) Tj
T*
(   - Phosphorylated Ensa acts as an extraordinarily tight, stoichiometric inhibitor of PP2A-B55,) Tj
T*
(   completely shutting off substrate dephosphorylation.) Tj
T*
(   5. Systems Consequence \(Bistable Hysteresis\):) Tj
T*
(   This systems architecture converts a graded, continuous input \(cyclin B accumulation\) into an) Tj
T*
(   irreversible, all-or-none, bistable switch with zero intermediate states, driving the) Tj
T*
(   instantaneous, genome-wide execution of mitosis.) Tj
T*
