(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the structural organization and function of the Kinetochore, detailing the inner KMN network and the Ndc80 complex.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Structural Architecture of the Kinetochore and the KMN Network:) Tj
T*
(   1. Centromeric Chromatin Foundation:) Tj
T*
(   The kinetochore is a massive, multi-protein disc \(~100 MDa, > 100 distinct proteins\) assembled) Tj
T*
(   on centromeric heterochromatin:) Tj
T*
(   - Inner Kinetochore: Centromeric nucleosomes contain the histone H3 variant CENP-A \(Centromere) Tj
T*
(   Protein A\) instead of canonical H3.) Tj
T*
(   - The Constitutive Centromere-Associated Network \(CCAN\): A 16-subunit complex \(CENP-C, CENP-T,) Tj
T*
(   CENP-W, CENP-S, CENP-X, etc.\) assembled stably on CENP-A chromatin throughout the entire cell) Tj
T*
(   cycle, forming the physical docking pad for the outer kinetochore.) Tj
T*
(   2. The KMN Outer Kinetochore Network:) Tj
T*
(   During prophase, CCAN components recruit the KMN network, the core structural engine that) Tj
T*
(   physically captures spindle microtubules:) Tj
T*
(   - KMN is composed of three interconnected subcomplexes: KNL1 complex, Mis12 complex, and Ndc80) Tj
T*
(   complex.) Tj
T*
(   - Mis12 Complex \(Mis12 - Dsn1 - Nnf1 - Nsl1\): A 22 nm rod acting as the central molecular) Tj
T*
(   adapter bridging CENP-C to Ndc80 and KNL1.) Tj
T*
(   - KNL1 Complex \(KNL1 - Zwint\): Long scaffold that coordinates the Spindle Assembly Checkpoint) Tj
T*
