(   3. The Ndc80 Complex \(The Primary Microtubule Coupler\):) Tj
T*
(   A 57 nm elongated, rigid heterotetramer consisting of two heterodimers joined in an) Tj
T*
(   antiparallel coiled-coil rod:) Tj
T*
(   - Head Domain \(Microtubule-Binding Face\): Composed of the globular N-terminal Calponin Homology) Tj
T*
(   \(CH\) domains of Ndc80 \(Hec1\) and Nuf2.) Tj
T*
(   - Tail Domain \(Kinetochore-Facing\): Composed of Spc24 and Spc25, forming a globular head that) Tj
T*
(   anchors into the Mis12 complex.) Tj
T*
(   - The Basic N-terminal Tail: The extreme N-terminus of Ndc80 contains an intrinsically) Tj
T*
(   disordered, basic tail \(~80 amino acids\) carrying positive charges that bind electrostatically) Tj
T*
(   to the acidic, negatively charged C-terminal 'E-hooks' of alpha- and beta-tubulin) Tj
T*
(   protofilaments.) Tj
T*
(   - Cooperativity: Multiple Ndc80 complexes oligomerize along a single microtubule plus-end,) Tj
T*
(   forming a flexible multivalent sleeve capable of maintaining mechanical attachment during both) Tj
T*
(   polymerization and curling depolymerization.) Tj
