(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Error Correction mechanism of Kinetochore-Microtubule Attachments mediated by Aurora B Kinase and Tension Sensing.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Kinetochore Error Correction and Aurora B Tension Sensing:) Tj
T*
(   1. Types of Kinetochore-Microtubule Attachments:) Tj
T*
(   - Amphitelic Attachment \(Correct / Bipolar\): Sister kinetochores attach to microtubules) Tj
T*
(   emanating from opposite spindle poles; generates balanced mechanical tension.) Tj
T*
(   - Monotelic Attachment: Only one sister kinetochore is attached.) Tj
T*
(   - Syntelic Attachment \(Aberrant\): Both sister kinetochores attach to microtubules from the SAME) Tj
T*
(   spindle pole. Zero tension.) Tj
T*
(   - Merotelic Attachment \(Aberrant\): A single kinetochore attaches simultaneously to microtubules) Tj
T*
(   from BOTH spindle poles.) Tj
T*
(   2. Spatial Separation Model of Aurora B Kinase:) Tj
T*
(   Aurora B is the catalytic kinase core of the Chromosomal Passenger Complex \(CPC: Aurora B,) Tj
T*
(   INCENP, Survivin, Borealin\):) Tj
T*
(   - Location: The CPC is anchored at the inner centromeric chromatin between the two sister) Tj
T*
(   kinetochores via Survivin binding to phosphorylated histone H3 \(Thr-3\) and Borealin binding to) Tj
T*
(   phosphorylated histone H2A \(Thr-120\).) Tj
T*
(   - Reach of the Kinase: Aurora B can only phosphorylate substrates located within a defined) Tj
T*
(   spatial radius \(~30-50 nm\) from the inner centromere.) Tj
T*
(   3. Tension-Dependent Release Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   - Unattached or Syntelic State \(No Mechanical Tension\):) Tj
T*
(   Without opposing poleward forces, sister kinetochores remain in close proximity \(~0.7 microns) Tj
T*
(   apart\).) Tj
T*
(   The outer kinetochore Ndc80 complex sits within the active reach of Aurora B.) Tj
T*
(   Aurora B phosphorylates up to 9 serine/threonine residues on the basic N-terminal tail of) Tj
T*
(   Ndc80.) Tj
T*
(   The introduction of negative phosphate charges electrostatically repels the acidic tubulin) Tj
T*
(   E-hook, destabilizing the attachment and causing microtubule detachment. This gives the) Tj
T*
(   kinetochore another chance to capture an opposing microtubule!) Tj
T*
(   - Amphitelic State \(Bipolar Mechanical Tension\):) Tj
T*
(   Microtubules from opposing poles pull on the sister kinetochores with forces of 100-700 pN.) Tj
T*
(   This mechanical tension stretches the elastic centromeric chromatin, physically pulling the) Tj
T*
(   outer kinetochore Ndc80 complex > 1.2 microns away from the inner centromere, placing it) Tj
T*
(   OUTSIDE the spatial reach of Aurora B!) Tj
T*
