12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the molecular mechanism of the Spindle Assembly Checkpoint \(SAC\), explaining MCC generation and APC/C-Cdc20 inhibition.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Spindle Assembly Checkpoint \(SAC\) and Mitotic Checkpoint Complex \(MCC\):) Tj
T*
(   1. The Checkpoint Function:) Tj
T*
(   The SAC is an exquisite surveillance mechanism that monitors the attachment and tension of) Tj
T*
(   kinetochores, ensuring that anaphase onset is strictly prevented until every single chromosome) Tj
T*
(   has achieved stable, amphitelic bipolar attachment. A single unattached kinetochore is) Tj
T*
(   sufficient to arrest the entire cell in metaphase!) Tj
T*
(   2. Catalytic Signal Amplification at Unattached Kinetochores:) Tj
T*
(   - Mps1 Kinase Recruitment: Mps1 binds the Ndc80 complex on unattached kinetochores and) Tj
T*
(   phosphorylates multiple MELT motifs on the KNL1 scaffold.) Tj
T*
(   - Recruitment of Checkpoint Proteins: Phospho-MELT motifs recruit Bub3-Bub1 and Bub3-BubR1) Tj
T*
(   heterodimers, which in turn recruit the Mad1-Mad2 complex.) Tj
T*
(   3. The Mad2 Conformational Template Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   - Mad2 exists in two native conformational topologies: Open Mad2 \(O-Mad2\) in the cytosol, and) Tj
T*
(   Closed Mad2 \(C-Mad2\).) Tj
T*
(   - A stable, constitutive C-Mad2 molecule is bound to Mad1 at the unattached kinetochore, acting) Tj
T*
(   as a physical template.) Tj
T*
(   - Soluble O-Mad2 binds the Mad1-bound C-Mad2, undergoing a catalyzed conformational) Tj
T*
(   rearrangement into active C-Mad2.) Tj
T*
(   - Newly formed C-Mad2 entraps the mitotic activator protein Cdc20 by wrapping its flexible) Tj
T*
(   C-terminal safety-belt loop around a conserved peptide segment of Cdc20.) Tj
T*
(   4. Assembly of the Mitotic Checkpoint Complex \(MCC\):) Tj
T*
(   The C-Mad2-Cdc20 dimer binds BubR1 and Bub3 to assemble the tetrameric Mitotic Checkpoint) Tj
T*
(   Complex:) Tj
T*
(   MCC = [BubR1 - Bub3 - Mad2 - Cdc20].) Tj
T*
(   The MCC diffuses into the nucleoplasm, functioning as a diffusible catalytic inhibitor.) Tj
T*
(   5. Molecular Inhibition of the APC/C:) Tj
T*
(   - The Anaphase-Promoting Complex / Cyclosome \(APC/C\) is a massive 1.2 MDa E3 ubiquitin ligase) Tj
T*
(   that requires Cdc20 as an activator to recognize destruction boxes \(D-boxes\) on Securin and) Tj
T*
(   Cyclin B.) Tj
T*
(   - The MCC binds APC/C as a pseudo-substrate inhibitor: BubR1 inserts its own D-box and KEN-box) Tj
T*
(   into the substrate-binding groove of Cdc20, completely blocking substrate access and preventing) Tj
T*
(   APC/C activation.) Tj
T*
(   6. Silencing the SAC upon Attachment:) Tj
T*
(   When microtubules attach, motor proteins \(dynein\) strip Mad1, Mad2, and Mps1 off the) Tj
T*
(   kinetochore \('kinetochore shedding'\), moving them toward spindle poles.) Tj
T*
(   The AAA+ ATPase p31-comet and TRIP13 disassemble remaining MCC complexes, freeing Cdc20 to) Tj
T*
(   activate APC/C and trigger anaphase within minutes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
