(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the stages of Meiosis I and II, highlighting the molecular architecture of the Synaptonemal Complex and Chiasma resolution.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Comprehensive Molecular Mechanics of Meiotic Division:) Tj
T*
(   1. Meiotic Specialization:) Tj
T*
(   Meiosis reduces the diploid genome \(2n\) to haploid gametes \(1n\) through a single round of) Tj
T*
(   S-phase replication followed by two successive chromosome segregations:) Tj
T*
(   - Meiosis I: Segregation of homologous chromosomes \(reductional\).) Tj
T*
(   - Meiosis II: Segregation of sister chromatids \(equational\).) Tj
T*
(   2. The Five Substages of Prophase I:) Tj
T*
(   - Leptotene: Chromatin begins condensation; sister chromatids assemble along a shared axial) Tj
T*
(   core. Spo11 topoisomerase introduces programmed double-strand DNA breaks \(DSBs\).) Tj
T*
(   - Zygotene: Homologous chromosomes find each other and begin physical pairing \(Synapsis\).) Tj
T*
(   Assembly of the Synaptonemal Complex \(SC\) begins.) Tj
T*
(   - Pachytene: Full synapsis is achieved along the entire length of homologous bivalents. Genetic) Tj
T*
(   crossing over \(homologous recombination\) occurs, mediated by Rad51/Dmc1 recombinases and) Tj
T*
(   Holliday junction resolvases.) Tj
T*
(   - Diplotene: The synaptonemal complex disassembles. Homologs desynapse and repel each other,) Tj
T*
(   remaining physically held together only at sites of crossing over, visible as X-shaped) Tj
T*
(   Chiasmata.) Tj
T*
(   - Diakinesis: Chromosomes achieve maximal condensation; nucleolus disappears; nuclear envelope) Tj
T*
