T*
(   A tripartite, ladder-like macromolecular protein scaffold:) Tj
T*
(   - Two Lateral Elements \(LEs\): Formed along the axial cores of each homolog, composed of SYCP2) Tj
T*
(   and SYCP3, anchoring cohesin complexes containing meiotic kleisin Rec8.) Tj
T*
(   - Central Element \(CE\): Located midway across a 100 nm gap, assembled from SYCE1, SYCE2, SYCE3,) Tj
T*
(   and TEX12.) Tj
T*
(   - Transverse Filaments \(TFs\): Formed by homodimers of SYCP1 oriented in an antiparallel) Tj
T*
(   zip-like fashion, with their C-termini anchored in the lateral elements and their N-termini) Tj
T*
(   interdigitating in the central element.) Tj
T*
(   4. Meiosis I vs. Meiosis II Segregation Logic:) Tj
T*
(   - In Anaphase I: Kinetochores of sister chromatids are co-oriented toward the SAME spindle pole) Tj
T*
(   \(mono-orientation driven by the Meikin complex\). Shugoshin-2 \(Sgo2\) recruits PP2A phosphatase) Tj
T*
(   to centromeric Rec8 cohesin, shielding it from separase cleavage.) Tj
T*
(   - Separase cleaves ONLY arm cohesin, resolving chiasmata and allowing homologous chromosomes to) Tj
T*
(   separate to opposite poles, while sister chromatids remain linked at centromeres!) Tj
T*
(   - In Anaphase II: Equational division. Kinetochores bi-orient; Sgo2 is absent; separase cleaves) Tj
T*
(   the remaining centromeric Rec8, allowing sister chromatid disjunction into four genetically) Tj
