(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the molecular mechanics of Cytokinesis in animal cells, detailing Centralspindlin, ECT2, RhoA, the Contractile Ring, and ESCRT-III Abscission.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Molecular Cascade of Animal Cytokinesis:) Tj
T*
(   1. Spatial Specification of the Division Plane \(Anaphase\):) Tj
T*
(   During late anaphase, overlapping antiparallel interpolar microtubules assemble into the) Tj
T*
(   tightly packed Central Spindle \(Spindle Midzone\):) Tj
T*
(   - The heterotetrameric Centralspindlin complex \(composed of two MKLP1 kinesin-6 motor subunits) Tj
T*
(   and two MgcRacGAP / CYK-4 subunits\) accumulates at the midzone plus-ends, organized by Aurora B) Tj
T*
(   and Plk1 kinases.) Tj
T*
(   - Centralspindlin recruits the guanine nucleotide exchange factor ECT2 to the midzone.) Tj
T*
(   2. Equatorial Activation of RhoA:) Tj
T*
(   - ECT2 transfers to the overlying equatorial cortex, where it catalyzes GDP-to-GTP exchange on) Tj
T*
(   the small GTPase RhoA, generating a sharp, localized band of active RhoA-GTP at the cell) Tj
T*
(   equator.) Tj
T*
(   - Concurrently, MgcRacGAP inactivates Rac1, suppressing branched actin polymerization at the) Tj
T*
(   equator.) Tj
T*
(   3. Contractile Ring Assembly and Ingression:) Tj
T*
(   Active RhoA binds and activates two critical downstream effectors:) Tj
T*
(   - Formin \(mDia1 / DIAPH1\): Binds RhoA, nucleating the de novo polymerization of long,) Tj
T*
(   unbranched actin filaments oriented parallel to the equatorial plane.) Tj
T*
(   - Rho-Associated Kinase \(ROCK\): Directly phosphorylates the regulatory light chain of) Tj
T*
(   non-muscle Myosin II \(Ser-19\) and inhibits Myosin Light Chain Phosphatase \(MLCP\), activating) Tj
T*
(   Myosin II bipolar filament assembly.) Tj
T*
(   - Antiparallel sliding of actin filaments by myosin II generates constrictive hoop stress,) Tj
T*
(   pulling the plasma membrane inward to form the deepening Cleavage Furrow.) Tj
T*
(   4. Midbody Formation and ESCRT-III Abscission:) Tj
T*
(   - Furrow ingression compresses central spindle microtubules into an electron-dense, narrow) Tj
T*
(   intercellular bridge called the Midbody \(~1 micron diameter\).) Tj
T*
(   - Centrosomal protein CEP55 is recruited to the midbody ring, where it recruits TSG101) Tj
T*
(   \(ESCRT-I\) and ALIX.) Tj
T*
(   - ESCRT-I and ALIX nucleate the polymerization of ESCRT-III \(CHMP4B\) filaments, which form) Tj
T*
