T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Li-Fraumeni Syndrome and the Dominant-Negative Mechanism of TP53 Mutations:) Tj
T*
(   1. Genetic Etiology of Li-Fraumeni Syndrome \(LFS\):) Tj
T*
(   LFS is a rare, devastating autosomal dominant hereditary cancer predisposition syndrome caused) Tj
T*
(   by germline heterozygous mutations in the TP53 tumor suppressor gene:) Tj
T*
(   - Affected individuals have a lifetime cancer risk approaching 90% by age 60, characterized by) Tj
T*
(   early-onset sarcomas, breast cancers, brain tumors \(gliomas\), adrenocortical carcinomas, and) Tj
