T*
(   2. The Unique Mutation Profile of p53:) Tj
T*
(   Unlike classic tumor suppressors \(e.g., RB1, APC, BRCA1\) which are inactivated by nonsense,) Tj
T*
(   frameshift, or deletion mutations leading to protein absence:) Tj
T*
(   - Over 75% of p53 mutations in cancer are single amino acid Missense Mutations clustering) Tj
T*
(   within the sequence-specific DNA-Binding Domain \(DBD, residues 102-292\).) Tj
T*
(   - Six 'Hotspot' residues account for > 30% of all mutations: Arg-175, Gly-245, Arg-248,) Tj
T*
(   Arg-249, Arg-273, Arg-282.) Tj
T*
(   - Contact Mutants \(e.g., R248, R273\): Alter amino acids directly contacting the DNA phosphate) Tj
T*
(   backbone or major groove.) Tj
T*
(   - Conformational / Structural Mutants \(e.g., R175, G245\): Disrupt local folding or coordinate) Tj
T*
(   zinc binding, destabilizing the beta-sandwich scaffold.) Tj
T*
(   3. The Dominant-Negative Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   - Active p53 must assemble as a homotetramer \(a dimer of dimers\) to bind its consensus DNA) Tj
T*
(   response elements.) Tj
T*
(   - In heterozygous cells carrying one wild-type and one missense mutant allele, statistical) Tj
T*
(   subunit mixing produces tetramers containing 0, 1, 2, 3, or 4 mutant monomers.) Tj
T*
(   - Incorporation of even a single mutant subunit into the tetrameric complex distorts the) Tj
T*
(   spatial orientation of the DNA-binding surfaces, inactivating the entire tetramer!) Tj
T*
(   - Out of 16 possible tetramer configurations, only 1/16 \(6.25%\) is composed of pure wild-type) Tj
T*
(   subunits. Thus, the mutant allele exerts a dominant-negative poisoning effect over the) Tj
T*
(   remaining wild-type allele even before Loss of Heterozygosity \(LOH\) occurs.) Tj
T*
(   4. Gain-of-Function \(GOF\) Oncogenic Properties:) Tj
T*
(   Mutant p53 proteins escape MDM2-mediated degradation and accumulate to massive levels. Many) Tj
T*
(   missense mutants physically interact with other transcription factors \(p63, p73\), inhibiting) Tj
T*
(   their pro-apoptotic functions, or bind novel genomic loci to upregulate pro-metastatic genes,) Tj
T*
(   conferring drug resistance and invasive properties.) Tj
T*
