(   4. The Two Competing Molecular Clocks \(Bcl-2 vs. Cyclin B\):) Tj
T*
(   During prolonged mitotic arrest, two independent, competing biochemical degradation timers run) Tj
T*
(   concurrently:) Tj
T*
(   - Death Clock \(Apoptotic Priming\): Active CDK1 phosphorylates anti-apoptotic proteins Mcl-1 and) Tj
T*
(   Bcl-xL, targeting Mcl-1 for ubiquitin-mediated degradation by the SCF-FBW7 complex.) Tj
T*
(   Concurrently, pro-apoptotic BH3-only proteins \(Bim, Noxa\) accumulate.) Tj
T*
(   - Survival Clock \(Mitotic Slippage\): Despite SAC engagement, a slow, continuous leak of Cyclin) Tj
T*
(   B degradation occurs via residual APC/C activity \('mitotic slippage'\).) Tj
T*
(   - Outcome: If Mcl-1 levels fall below the critical survival threshold before Cyclin B drops,) Tj
T*
(   Bax/Bak are activated, inducing MOMP and explosive caspase-dependent apoptosis directly from) Tj
T*
(   mitotic arrest!) Tj
T*
(   - If mitotic slippage occurs first, the cell exits mitosis without division, becoming a) Tj
T*
(   tetraploid G1 cell that is subsequently cleared by p53-dependent senescence or apoptosis.) Tj
