12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the structural mechanics of Condensin I and II complexes in hierarchical chromosome condensation during prophase.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Molecular Architecture and Loop Extrusion by Condensin I and II:) Tj
T*
(   1. The SMC Protein Core Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   Condensins are conserved multi-subunit ring-shaped protein complexes belonging to the) Tj
T*
(   Structural Maintenance of Chromosomes \(SMC\) family:) Tj
T*
(   - Both Condensin I and Condensin II share an identical SMC core: an Smc2-Smc4 heterodimer.) Tj
T*
(   - Each SMC protein consists of an 50 nm antiparallel coiled-coil arm with a globular) Tj
T*
(   dimerization 'Hinge' at one end and an ATP-binding catalytic 'Head' \(ABC-like ATPase\) at the) Tj
T*
(   other.) Tj
T*
(   - The two heads are bridged by a non-SMC kleisin subunit, forming a closed topological ring.) Tj
T*
(   2. Distinct Auxiliary Subunits and Spatial Localization:) Tj
T*
(   - Condensin I: Contains the kleisin CAP-H and two HEAT-repeat subunits \(CAP-D2, CAP-G\).) Tj
T*
(   Excluded from the nucleus during interphase by the nuclear envelope; gains access to) Tj
T*
(   chromosomes only after Nuclear Envelope Breakdown \(NEBD\) in prometaphase.) Tj
T*
(   - Condensin II: Contains the kleisin CAP-H2 and HEAT subunits \(CAP-D3, CAP-G2\). Resides) Tj
T*
(   constitutively inside the nucleus throughout interphase, initiating the earliest stages of) Tj
T*
(   chromosome axial shortening in early prophase.) Tj
T*
(   3. The Loop Extrusion Molecular Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   Recent single-molecule biophysical experiments demonstrate that condensin functions as an) Tj
T*
(   ATP-fueled molecular motor that actively reels in DNA:) Tj
T*
(   - The condensin ring binds a segment of double-stranded DNA.) Tj
T*
(   - Sequential cycles of ATP binding, head engagement, and ATP hydrolysis drive continuous,) Tj
T*
(   processive reeling of DNA through the ring at speeds up to 1,500 base pairs/second.) Tj
T*
(   - This extrudes DNA into expanding loops without changing topological writhe.) Tj
T*
(   4. Two-Tiered Hierarchical Chromosome Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   - Condensin II acts first along the central longitudinal axis, extruding giant consecutive) Tj
T*
(   loops \(~200-400 kb\) to establish a rigid helical core scaffold.) Tj
T*
(   - Once the nuclear envelope breaks down, Condensin I binds, nesting smaller secondary sub-loops) Tj
T*
(   \(~80-100 kb\) within the primary loops.) Tj
T*
(   - Working cooperatively with Topoisomerase IIalpha \(which decatenates intertwined strands\),) Tj
T*
(   condensin compacts the 2-meter-long human genome by > 10,000-fold into rigid, rod-shaped) Tj
T*
(   cylindrical mitotic chromatids capable of segregation without entanglement.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
