(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the role of Polo-Like Kinase 1 \(Plk1\) as a master orchestrator of mitotic transitions.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Polo-Like Kinase 1 \(Plk1\) Orchestration Across Mitosis:) Tj
T*
(   1. Structural Organization of Plk1:) Tj
T*
(   Plk1 consists of an N-terminal Ser/Thr kinase domain and a unique C-terminal non-catalytic) Tj
T*
(   Polo-Box Domain \(PBD\) composed of two polo boxes:) Tj
T*
(   - The PBD acts as an intramolecular inhibitory clamp that folds back over the kinase domain in) Tj
T*
(   basal state.) Tj
T*
(   - Priming Phosphorylation: Upstream kinases \(e.g., CDK1\) phosphorylate substrates on) Tj
T*
(   Ser-[pSer/pThr]-Pro motifs. The PBD recognizes and binds this pre-phosphorylated docking motif,) Tj
T*
(   relieving auto-inhibition and targeting Plk1 precisely to specific subcellular structures) Tj
T*
(   \(centrosomes, kinetochores, spindle midzone\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Five Master Mitotic Transitions Governed by Plk1:) Tj
T*
(   - Centrosome Maturation and Separation \(G2/M\): Plk1 phosphorylates pericentriolar material) Tj
T*
(   \(PCM\) scaffolding proteins \(pericentrin, NEDD1\), recruiting gamma-tubulin ring complexes to) Tj
T*
(   expand microtubule-nucleating capacity. Concurrently, it activates Nek2 to sever the) Tj
T*
(   intercentriolar protein tether, driving centrosome separation.) Tj
T*
(   - Mitotic Entry Trigger: Plk1 phosphorylates Cdc25C on Ser-198 to activate its phosphatase) Tj
T*
(   function and phosphorylates Wee1 to mark it for SCF-beta-TrCP degradation, igniting the) Tj
T*
(   explosive activation of MPF.) Tj
T*
(   - Cohesin Removal via the Prophase Pathway: Phosphorylates the SA2 \(Scc3\) subunit of cohesin) Tj
T*
(   along chromosome arms, enabling Wapl to release cohesin rings from DNA without separase) Tj
T*
(   cleavage.) Tj
T*
(   - Kinetochore-Microtubule Attachment: Phosphorylates Bub1, BubR1, and KNL1, recruiting) Tj
T*
(   checkpoint components and stabilizing amphitelic attachments.) Tj
T*
(   - Cytokinesis Initiation: During anaphase, Plk1 localizes to the central spindle,) Tj
T*
(   phosphorylating the MgcRacGAP subunit of Centralspindlin, creating the recruitment docking site) Tj
T*
(   for the RhoGEF ECT2 to activate RhoA.) Tj
T*
