(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the structural organization and function of the Midbody during cytokinesis and explain how the NoCut checkpoint delays abscission.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Midbody Architecture and the NoCut Abscission Checkpoint:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Midbody \(Flemming Body\) Ultrastructure:) Tj
T*
(   The midbody is a dense, protein-rich organelle formed by the compaction of antiparallel central) Tj
T*
(   spindle microtubules at the center of the intercellular bridge connecting two daughter cells) Tj
T*
(   \(~1 micron diameter, ~3 microns long\):) Tj
T*
(   - Midbody Core \(Dark Zone\): A dense protein matrix containing bundled overlapping microtubule) Tj
T*
(   plus-ends, kinesin motors \(MKLP1, MKLP2\), Plk1, and scaffolding proteins \(PRC1, CEP55\).) Tj
T*
(   - Abscission Site: Located ~1 micron adjacent to the central midbody core, where the plasma) Tj
T*
(   membrane is narrowed to a thin stalk \(< 100 nm\) and cleaved.) Tj
T*
(   2. The Abscission Machinery \(ESCRT-III Recruitment\):) Tj
T*
(   - As Plk1 activity declines at mitotic exit, CEP55 is dephosphorylated, allowing it to dock at) Tj
T*
(   the midbody core.) Tj
T*
(   - CEP55 recruits the ESCRT-I component TSG101 and the adaptor ALIX.) Tj
T*
(   - These recruit ESCRT-III \(CHMP4B\), which polymerizes into conical, spiral spring-like) Tj
T*
(   filaments that extend laterally along the inner face of the bridge membrane.) Tj
T*
(   - CHMP4B recruits the microtubule-severing AAA+ ATPase Spastin to dismantle underlying) Tj
T*
(   microtubules, clearing the lumen for final membrane fission.) Tj
T*
(   3. The NoCut Abscission Checkpoint \(Chromatin Bridge Surveillance\):) Tj
T*
(   If chromosome segregation fails and an under-replicated or tangled chromosome arm remains) Tj
T*
(   trapped across the cleavage furrow \(a chromatin bridge\), premature abscission would cause DNA) Tj
T*
(   double-strand breakage, translocation, and aneuploidy:) Tj
T*
(   - The NoCut checkpoint senses chromatin bridges via Aurora B kinase, which remains) Tj
T*
(   constitutively active at the midbody in the presence of trapped DNA.) Tj
T*
(   - Active Aurora B directly phosphorylates the CHMP4C subunit of ESCRT-III on Ser-210.) Tj
T*
(   - Phospho-CHMP4C halts further spiral polymer assembly and blocks Spastin recruitment, freezing) Tj
T*
(   the abscission machinery in a reversible standby state.) Tj
T*
(   - Abscission is delayed until Topoisomerase II and DNA repair helicases resolve the bridge,) Tj
T*
(   clearing chromatin from the cleavage plane, whereupon Aurora B inactivates and abscission) Tj
T*
(   proceeds safely.) Tj
T*
