(   2. The Voltage-Sensing Mechanism of PINK1:) Tj
T*
(   PINK1 \(PTEN-Induced Kinase 1\) is a Ser/Thr kinase that acts as an electrochemical voltmeter of) Tj
T*
(   the inner mitochondrial membrane:) Tj
T*
(   - In Healthy Mitochondria \(High Membrane Potential Delta Psi\): Newly synthesized PINK1 is) Tj
T*
(   continuously imported across both membranes via TOM and TIM23 complexes. The inner membrane) Tj
T*
(   protease PARL cleaves PINK1 within its transmembrane domain, releasing a 52 kDa truncated) Tj
T*
(   fragment that diffuses into the cytosol and is rapidly degraded by the N-end rule) Tj
T*
(   ubiquitin-proteasome pathway. Healthy mitochondria maintain undetectable basal PINK1!) Tj
T*
(   - In Damaged/Depolarized Mitochondria \(Delta Psi Collapsed\): Loss of the proton motive force) Tj
T*
(   halts electrophoretic import through TIM23. PARL cannot cleave PINK1. Full-length, active 64) Tj
T*
(   kDa PINK1 accumulates on the outer mitochondrial membrane \(OMM\) as an active homodimeric) Tj
T*
(   complex associated with TOM40.) Tj
T*
(   3. Parkin Recruitment and Ubiquitin Phosphorylation:) Tj
T*
(   - Accumulated PINK1 autophosphorylates and phosphorylates pre-existing Ubiquitin molecules) Tj
T*
(   attached to OMM proteins at a conserved serine residue: Ser-65 \(forming Phospho-Ubiquitin\).) Tj
T*
(   - Phospho-Ubiquitin serves as an extraordinarily high-affinity receptor that recruits the) Tj
T*
(   cytosolic E3 ubiquitin ligase Parkin \(PRKN\) from the cytoplasm to the damaged mitochondrion.) Tj
T*
(   - PINK1 directly phosphorylates the ubiquitin-like \(UBL\) domain of Parkin \(at Ser-65\),) Tj
T*
(   relieving Parkin's auto-inhibition and activating its E3 ligase activity.) Tj
T*
(   4. Feed-Forward Ubiquitin Amplification:) Tj
T*
(   Active Parkin decorates numerous outer membrane proteins \(Mfn1, Mfn2, VDAC, Miro\) with dense) Tj
T*
(   polyubiquitin chains. PINK1 phosphorylates these newly added ubiquitins, recruiting more) Tj
T*
(   Parkin, creating a rapid, self-amplifying feed-forward loop.) Tj
T*
(   5. Autophagosomal Clearance:) Tj
T*
(   Phospho-ubiquitin chains recruit autophagy adaptor proteins \(OPTN, NDP52, p62\) via their) Tj
T*
(   ubiquitin-binding domains. Adaptors bind LC3-II on expanding isolation membranes, engulfing the) Tj
T*
(   damaged mitochondrion into an autophagosome targeted for lysosomal degradation.) Tj
T*
(   6. Clinical Connection:) Tj
T*
(   Autosomal recessive loss-of-function mutations in PINK1 \(PARK6\) or PRKN \(PARK2\) cause) Tj
T*
(   early-onset familial Parkinson's disease due to progressive accumulation of damaged) Tj
T*
(   mitochondria and ROS-induced death of dopaminergic neurons in the substantia nigra.) Tj
T*
