(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss the molecular regulation of the Spindle Position Checkpoint \(SPOC\) and the Centrosome Duplication cycle.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Centrosome Duplication Cycle and the Spindle Position Checkpoint \(SPOC\):) Tj
T*
(   1. The Centrosome Duplication Cycle:) Tj
T*
(   The centrosome is the primary microtubule organizing center \(MTOC\) of animal cells, consisting) Tj
T*
(   of a pair of orthogonally oriented centrioles \(mother and daughter\) embedded in pericentriolar) Tj
T*
(   material \(PCM\):) Tj
T*
(   - G1 Phase \(Centriole Disengagement\): Separase and Plk1 cleave the proteinaceous tether) Tj
T*
(   connecting the mother and daughter centrioles \('disengagement'\), licensing them for a single) Tj
T*
(   round of duplication.) Tj
T*
(   - G1/S Transition \(Procentriole Assembly\): Plk4 kinase localizes to a single site on the parent) Tj
T*
(   centriole wall. Plk4 phosphorylates STIL, recruiting SAS-6. SAS-6 oligomerizes into a nine-fold) Tj
T*
(   symmetrical cartwheel hub, the structural foundation of the nascent procentriole.) Tj
T*
(   - S and G2 Phases \(Elongation\): SAS-4 \(CPAP\) directs the polymerization of nine triplet) Tj
T*
(   microtubules along the cartwheel, elongating the daughter centriole.) Tj
T*
(   - Mitotic Entry \(Maturation and Separation\): Plk1 and Aurora A recruit massive amounts of PCM) Tj
T*
(   \(pericentrin, gamma-tubulin ring complexes\). Eg5 \(Kinesin-5\) separates the duplicated) Tj
T*
(   centrosomes to opposite sides of the nucleus to form spindle poles.) Tj
T*
(   2. The Spindle Position Checkpoint \(SPOC\):) Tj
T*
