(   In asymmetric cell divisions \(e.g., budding yeast and mammalian stem cells\), the mitotic) Tj
T*
(   spindle must align precisely along the polarity axis to ensure unequal partitioning of) Tj
T*
(   developmental determinants:) Tj
T*
(   - The Kinase Signaling Cascade \(Bub2-Bfa1\): The GAP complex Bub2-Bfa1 localizes to spindle) Tj
T*
(   poles, maintaining the small GTPase Tem1 in an inactive GDP-bound state, preventing mitotic) Tj
T*
(   exit network \(MEN\) activation as long as the spindle is misaligned.) Tj
T*
(   - Alignment Trigger: When the spindle properly aligns and the daughter spindle pole migrates) Tj
T*
(   across the bud neck into the daughter cell, Tem1 encounters its activator Lte1 \(localized) Tj
T*
(   exclusively in the daughter cortex\).) Tj
T*
(   - Active Tem1-GTP triggers the protein kinase Cdc15 and Dbf2, driving release of Cdc14) Tj
T*
(   phosphatase from the nucleolus to dephosphorylate CDK1 substrates, enabling exit from mitosis) Tj
