(   [Problem Statement]: Explain how the SCF \(Skp1-Cullin-F-box\) ubiquitin ligase complex regulates cell cycle transitions and contrast its substrate targeting with the APC/C.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Mechanistic Comparison of SCF and APC/C Ubiquitin Ligases:) Tj
T*
(   1. Structural Architecture of the SCF Complex:) Tj
T*
(   The SCF complex is a modular multi-subunit Cullin-RING E3 Ubiquitin Ligase \(CRL1\):) Tj
T*
(   - Cul1 \(Cullin-1\): A rigid, curved scaffold that separates the catalytic core from the) Tj
T*
(   substrate receptor by ~10 nm.) Tj
T*
(   - Rbx1 \(Roc1\): A RING-finger protein bound to the C-terminus of Cul1 that recruits) Tj
T*
(   ubiquitin-charged E2 enzymes \(Cdc34 / UbcH5\).) Tj
T*
(   - Skp1: An adaptor protein bound to the N-terminus of Cul1.) Tj
T*
(   - F-Box Protein: The variable substrate recognition subunit containing an F-box motif binding) Tj
T*
(   Skp1, and a C-terminal protein-interaction domain \(WD40 repeats or leucine-rich repeats\)) Tj
T*
(   binding specific substrates:) Tj
T*
(   - Skp2: Recognizes phosphorylated p27 \(Kip1\).) Tj
T*
(   - beta-TrCP: Recognizes phosphorylated I-kappa-B, Emi1, and Wee1.) Tj
T*
(   - Fbw7: Recognizes phosphorylated Cyclin E, Myc, Notch, and c-Jun.) Tj
T*
(   2. Substrate Targeting Logic \(Phosphorylation-Dependent Recognition\):) Tj
T*
(   - SCF operates via a 'Constitutively Active Ligase / Phosphorylated Substrate' paradigm:) Tj
T*
(   The SCF complex is enzymatically active throughout interphase. It CANNOT recognize) Tj
T*
(   unphosphorylated substrates!) Tj
T*
(   Substrates must first be phosphorylated on specific serine/threonine motifs \(termed) Tj
T*
(   Phosphodegrons\) by upstream CDKs or GSK-3 before being captured by the F-box receptor.) Tj
T*
(   3. Contrast with the APC/C \(Anaphase-Promoting Complex\):) Tj
T*
(   - Complexity: SCF is a small 4-subunit complex \(~150 kDa\); APC/C is a massive 15-subunit) Tj
T*
(   complex \(~1.2 MDa\).) Tj
T*
(   - Temporal Regulation: SCF activity is continuous, regulated by substrate availability; APC/C) Tj
T*
(   activity is strictly cell-cycle-regulated \(active only from metaphase through late G1 via) Tj
T*
(   sequential binding of activators Cdc20 and Cdh1\).) Tj
T*
(   - Recognition Logic: APC/C recognizes unmodified primary peptide sequences \(D-Boxes, KEN-boxes\)) Tj
T*
(   via its activators, and does not require substrate phosphorylation \(in fact, Cdh1 binding is) Tj
T*
(   inhibited by phosphorylation!\).) Tj
