(   1. The Conserved SMC Architectures:) Tj
T*
(   Both Cohesin and Condensin are evolutionary descendants of prokaryotic SMC homodimers, sharing) Tj
T*
(   a conserved ring-like structural topology:) Tj
T*
(   - SMC Heterodimers: Formed by two distinct SMC polypeptides \(Smc1-Smc3 in Cohesin; Smc2-Smc4 in) Tj
T*
(   Condensin\).) Tj
T*
(   - Each SMC monomer folds back on itself: its central amino acid sequence forms an antiparallel) Tj
T*
(   coiled-coil rod \(~50 nm long\), bringing the N- and C-termini together to form an ATP-binding) Tj
T*
(   cassette \(ABC-type\) catalytic 'Head' at one end, and a flexible dimerization 'Hinge' at the) Tj
T*
(   other.) Tj
T*
(   - Two SMC monomers heterodimerize at their hinges, while their heads are bridged by a non-SMC) Tj
T*
(   protein belonging to the Kleisin family, enclosing a large topological lumen capable of) Tj
T*
(   encircling DNA.) Tj
T*
(   2. Cohesin Complex Specialization:) Tj
T*
(   - Subunit Composition: Smc1, Smc3, Scc1 \(Rad21 / Mcd1 kleisin\), and Scc3 \(STAG1/2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Topological Action: Cohesin acts as an intermolecular topological clamp that entraps TWO) Tj
T*
(   double-stranded DNA molecules \(sister chromatids\) inside its 35 nm lumen, holding them together) Tj
T*
(   from S-phase until anaphase disjunction.) Tj
T*
(   - Loading and Unloading: Loaded onto DNA in telophase/G1 by the Scc2-Scc4 \(NIPBL-MAU2\) loading) Tj
T*
(   complex; dynamically removed in prophase by Wapl-Pds5, and definitively cleaved at anaphase) Tj
T*
(   onset by Separase.) Tj
T*
(   3. Condensin Complex Specialization:) Tj
T*
(   - Subunit Composition: Smc2, Smc4, CAP-H \(kleisin in Condensin I\) or CAP-H2 \(kleisin in) Tj
T*
(   Condensin II\), and two HEAT-repeat subunits.) Tj
T*
(   - Topological Action: Condensin acts as an INTRA-molecular loop-extruding motor. Instead of) Tj
T*
(   embracing two sister chromatids, a single condensin ring reels in a single double-stranded DNA) Tj
T*
(   fiber, generating expansive loops that drive 10,000-fold axial compaction of the chromosome) Tj
T*
(   into a rigid mitotic rod.) Tj
T*
