(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the molecular regulation of the Anaphase-Promoting Complex switch from APC/C-Cdc20 to APC/C-Cdh1 during mitotic exit.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Sequential Activation Switch from APC/C-Cdc20 to APC/C-Cdh1:) Tj
T*
(   1. Temporal Specialization:) Tj
T*
(   Exit from mitosis and maintenance of the G1 stable ground state require two sequential,) Tj
T*
(   overlapping waves of APC/C activity driven by two distinct WD40-repeat activator cofactors:) Tj
T*
(   - APC/C-Cdc20: Active from metaphase to early anaphase; initiates sister chromatid separation) Tj
T*
(   and partial cyclin degradation.) Tj
T*
(   - APC/C-Cdh1: Active from late anaphase through the entirety of G1 phase; finishes mitotic) Tj
T*
(   cyclin destruction, resets replication licensing competence, and prevents premature S-phase) Tj
T*
(   entry.) Tj
T*
(   2. The Phosphorylation Switch Gating Cdh1:) Tj
T*
(   The temporal transition between the two activators is strictly regulated by CDK1) Tj
T*
(   phosphorylation:) Tj
T*
(   - In S, G2, and early M phases: Cdh1 is phosphorylated on multiple N-terminal regulatory) Tj
T*
(   serines by active CDK1 and CDK2.) Tj
T*
(   - Phosphorylation introduces electrostatic repulsion that directly blocks Cdh1 from binding the) Tj
T*
(   APC/C core, keeping Cdh1 completely inactive in the cytoplasm!) Tj
T*
(   3. The Anaphase Hand-Off Cascade:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: In metaphase, once the SAC is satisfied, APC/C-Cdc20 degrades Securin and a) Tj
T*
(   significant fraction of Cyclin B.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: As Cyclin B levels plummet, CDK1 kinase activity drops precipitously.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3: Declining CDK1 activity allows the counteracting dual-specificity phosphatase Cdc14) Tj
T*
