(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the molecular mechanisms of the G2/M DNA Damage Checkpoint, detailing the roles of Chk1, Claspin, and 14-3-3 sigma.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Molecular Cascades of the G2/M DNA Damage Checkpoint:) Tj
T*
(   1. Physiological Objective:) Tj
T*
(   The G2/M DNA damage checkpoint prevents eukaryotic cells from entering mitosis with damaged,) Tj
T*
(   fragmented, or incompletely replicated chromosomes, preventing mitotic catastrophe and) Tj
T*
(   chromosomal shattering.) Tj
T*
(   2. Signal Transduction \(ATR - Claspin - Chk1\):) Tj
T*
(   - Ultraviolet irradiation, alkylating agents, or replication fork stalling generates extended) Tj
T*
(   regions of single-stranded DNA coated with RPA.) Tj
T*
(   - RPA recruits ATRIP-ATR, while the 9-1-1 clamp recruits the activator TopBP1.) Tj
T*
(   - Claspin is an essential checkpoint adaptor protein that binds both ATR and the inactive) Tj
T*
(   effector kinase Chk1.) Tj
T*
(   - ATR phosphorylates Claspin, which presents Chk1 to ATR for efficient phosphorylation on two) Tj
T*
(   conserved effector serines: Ser-317 and Ser-345.) Tj
T*
(   - Phosphorylated, active Chk1 dissociates from Claspin to diffuse throughout the nucleus.) Tj
T*
(   3. Inactivation of the Cdc25 Phosphatase Family:) Tj
T*
(   - Active Chk1 phosphorylates the dual-specificity phosphatase Cdc25C on Ser-216 \(and homologous) Tj
T*
(   sites on Cdc25B and Cdc25A\).) Tj
T*
(   - Phosphorylation of Ser-216 creates a canonical high-affinity consensus binding motif) Tj
T*
(   \(RSX[pS]XP\) recognized by the phosphoserine-binding adapter protein 14-3-3 sigma.) Tj
T*
(   - Binding of 14-3-3 sigma to Cdc25C:) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) Sterically blocks its catalytic phosphatase pocket, reducing its enzymatic activity;) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) Unmasks a nuclear export signal \(NES\) while masking its nuclear localization signal \(NLS\),) Tj
T*
(   driving rapid CRM1-mediated export of Cdc25C from the nucleus into the cytoplasm.) Tj
T*
(   4. Maintenance of Inhibitory CDK1 Phosphorylation:) Tj
T*
(   - With Cdc25C physically excluded from the nucleus, Wee1 kinase remains dominant, continuously) Tj
T*
(   maintaining inhibitory Tyr-15 phosphorylation on CDK1.) Tj
T*
