(   [Problem Statement]: Explain how the Anaphase-Promoting Complex \(APC/C\) recognizes its substrates via Destruction Boxes \(D-Box\) and KEN-Boxes.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Degron Architecture and Substrate Recognition by the APC/C:) Tj
T*
(   1. Structural Core of the APC/C:) Tj
T*
(   The Anaphase-Promoting Complex / Cyclosome is a massive crescent-shaped multimeric cullin-RING) Tj
T*
(   E3 ubiquitin ligase composed of 14 core subunits organized into two main sub-complexes:) Tj
T*
(   - The Catalytic Sub-complex: Cullin subunit Apc2, RING subunit Apc11 \(which recruits E2 enzymes) Tj
T*
(   UbcH10/Ube2C and Ube2S\), and the structural platform Apc1.) Tj
T*
(   - The TPR Sub-complex: Apc3, Apc6, Apc7, Apc8 forming an extensive tetratricopeptide repeat) Tj
T*
(   array that recruits the co-activator proteins Cdc20 and Cdh1.) Tj
T*
(   2. Degron Motifs on APC/C Targets:) Tj
T*
(   APC/C does not recognize phosphorylated substrates; instead, it directly binds specific short) Tj
T*
(   linear peptide motifs \(degrons\) embedded in flexible loops of target proteins:) Tj
T*
(   - The Destruction Box \(D-Box\): Consensus sequence R-X-X-L-X-X-X-X-N \(where R is arginine, L is) Tj
T*
(   leucine, N is asparagine, and X is any amino acid\). Examples: Cyclin B1, Securin, Geminin.) Tj
T*
(   - The KEN-Box: Consensus sequence K-E-N-X-X-X-[N/D] \(Lys-Glu-Asn\). Examples: Cdc20, Nek2A,) Tj
T*
(   Aurora A, TPX2.) Tj
T*
(   - Other Specialized Degrons: ABBA motif \(D-type cyclins, BubR1\) and O-box.) Tj
T*
(   3. Co-Receptor Bipartite Recognition Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   - Structural biology \(cryo-EM\) reveals that D-box recognition requires a cooperative bipartite) Tj
T*
(   co-receptor pocket formed at the junction between the WD40 domain of the activator \(Cdc20 or) Tj
T*
(   Cdh1\) and the core subunit Apc10!) Tj
T*
(   - The invariant Arginine and Leucine residues of the D-box insert into deep hydrophobic and) Tj
T*
(   electrostatic pockets shared across the activator-Apc10 interface.) Tj
T*
(   - The KEN-box binds exclusively to the top surface of the activator's WD40 propeller.) Tj
T*
(   - This bipartite requirement explains why neither the core APC/C alone nor free Cdc20 alone can) Tj
T*
(   bind substrates - binding occurs only upon correct holoenzyme assembly.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
