(   [Problem Statement]: Explain how the Aurora Kinase family \(Aurora A, B, and C\) coordinates centrosome maturation, spindle assembly, and cytokinesis.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Functional Specialization of the Aurora Kinase Family:) Tj
T*
(   1. Aurora A Kinase \(Centrosome and Spindle Pole Organizer\):) Tj
T*
(   - Subcellular Localization: Localizes to centrosomes from S-phase through early mitosis, and to) Tj
T*
(   spindle pole microtubules during metaphase.) Tj
T*
(   - Activation Mechanism: Autophosphorylates on its T-loop \(Thr-288\) upon binding its allosteric) Tj
T*
(   activator TPX2 \(Targeting Protein for Xklp2\), released from importins by Ran-GTP near) Tj
T*
(   chromosomes.) Tj
T*
(   - Mitotic Functions:) Tj
T*
(   - Drives centrosome maturation by phosphorylating TACC3 and Centrosomin/pericentrin, recruiting) Tj
T*
(   gamma-TuRCs.) Tj
T*
(   - Phosphorylates Kif2a and Eg5, promoting centrosome separation and bipolar spindle bipolarity.) Tj
T*
(   - Essential for G2/M mitotic entry; phosphorylates Plk1 within its activation loop \(Thr-210\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Aurora B Kinase \(The Chromosomal Passenger Kinase\):) Tj
T*
(   - Subcellular Localization: Displays dynamic 'passenger' redistribution: localizes to) Tj
T*
(   chromosome arms in prophase, concentrates at inner centromeres from prometaphase to metaphase,) Tj
T*
(   transfers to the central spindle midzone in anaphase, and focuses at the midbody during) Tj
T*
(   cytokinesis.) Tj
T*
(   - Complex Architecture: Functions as the enzymatic engine of the Chromosomal Passenger Complex) Tj
T*
(   \(CPC\) with INCENP, Survivin, and Borealin.) Tj
T*
(   - Functions: Orchestrates chromosome condensation \(histone H3 Ser-10/28 phosphorylation\),) Tj
T*
(   corrects erroneous kinetochore attachments lacking tension \(Ndc80 phosphorylation\), enforces) Tj
T*
(   the SAC, and regulates cleavage furrow ingression and the NoCut abscission checkpoint.) Tj
T*
(   3. Aurora C Kinase \(Meiotic Specialist\):) Tj
T*
(   - Highly homologous to Aurora B, but expressed almost exclusively in mammalian germ cells) Tj
T*
(   \(oocytes and spermatocytes\).) Tj
T*
(   - Substitutes for Aurora B in the CPC during meiotic maturation, ensuring proper bivalent) Tj
T*
(   alignment, chiasma stability, and polar body extrusion during oogenesis.) Tj
T*
