(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss the molecular composition of the Synaptonemal Complex and explain how the MutL-gamma resolvase complex executes crossover resolution.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Synaptonemal Complex and Crossover Resolution by MutL-gamma:) Tj
T*
(   1. Macromolecular Assembly of the Synaptonemal Complex \(SC\):) Tj
T*
(   The SC is a proteinaceous paracrystalline structure that physically zippers maternal and) Tj
T*
(   paternal homologous chromatids together during the pachytene stage of meiotic prophase I:) Tj
T*
(   - Lateral Elements \(LEs\): Formed by SYCP2 and SYCP3 along the axial cores of each homolog,) Tj
T*
(   anchoring the loop bases of chromatin via meiotic cohesin rings \(Rec8, RAD21L, SMC1beta,) Tj
T*
(   STAG3\).) Tj
