(   - Transverse Filaments \(TFs\): Transverse protein SYCP1 homodimers extend across the 100 nm) Tj
T*
(   central space. Their C-termini anchor into the lateral elements, while their coiled-coil) Tj
T*
(   N-termini meet in the center.) Tj
T*
(   - Central Element \(CE\): A longitudinal lattice of SYCE1, SYCE2, SYCE3, and TEX12 that) Tj
T*
(   polymerizes to stabilize the zipped transverse filaments.) Tj
T*
(   2. Double-Strand Break Repair Pathway \(The Canonical Crossover Pathway\):) Tj
T*
(   - Programmed DSBs introduced by Spo11 are resected to generate 3' single-stranded DNA tails.) Tj
T*
(   - Meiosis-specific recombinase Dmc1 and canonical Rad51 catalyze strand invasion into the) Tj
T*
(   non-sister homologous chromatid, forming a displacement loop \(D-loop\).) Tj
T*
(   - Second-end capture and DNA synthesis form a Double Holliday Junction \(dHJ\) intermediate.) Tj
T*
(   3. Biased Crossover Resolution by MutL-gamma \(Mlh1-Mlh3 Resolvase\):) Tj
T*
(   In mitotic DNA repair, Holliday junctions are non-crossover resolved to prevent genomic) Tj
T*
(   rearrangements. In contrast, meiosis strictly requires at least one Crossover per chromosome) Tj
T*
(   \(the 'Obligate Crossover'\) to establish physical chiasmata for accurate segregation:) Tj
T*
(   - The heterodimeric MutS-gamma complex \(Msh4-Msh5\) binds and stabilizes the double Holliday) Tj
T*
(   junction.) Tj
T*
(   - Msh4-Msh5 recruits the MutL-gamma endonuclease heterodimer, composed of Mlh1 and Mlh3.) Tj
T*
(   - Mlh3 contains a conserved metal-dependent DQHA\(X\)2E\(X\)4E nuclease motif.) Tj
T*
(   - Guided by the pro-crossover factor Exo1 and polymerizing PCNA clamps, MutL-gamma introduces) Tj
T*
(   asymmetric, coordinated single-strand nicks into two non-crossing strands of the dHJ, resolving) Tj
T*
(   the topological junctions exclusively into Crossover recombinant products with flanking) Tj
T*
(   chiasmata.) Tj
